# Car Builder
This project is a simple implementation of the **Builder Design Pattern** in Java 17.

The main product is a `Car`. I used the Builder Pattern because a car has many different properties and optional features. The car can be created step by step using method chaining.

The project contains two builders: `SportsCarBuilder` and `SUVCarBuilder`. Sports cars have 2 seats, 2 doors and require at least 250 hp. SUVs have 5 seats, 4 doors and all-wheel drive by default.

CarDirector contains several ready-to-use car configurations, while `Main` demonstrates how the builders work and also allows the user to create a car through the console.

  Project Structure
Caк — Product
CarBuilder — Builder interface
AbstractCarBuilder— common builder logic
SportsCarBuilder — builds sports cars
SUVCarBuilder — builds SUVs
CarDirector — provides predefined car configurations
Main — client and demo
How to Run
Make sure Java 17 is installed.
bash
javac -d out src/main/java/carbuilder/*.java
java -cp out carbuilder.Main
Example
Car car = new SUVCarBuilder()
        .setBrand("Toyota")
        .setModel("Land Cruiser")
        .setEngine("V6 Diesel", 280)
        .addOffRoadPackage()
        .build();
The project demonstrates step-by-step construction, method chaining, validation, and different types of cars using the Builder Pattern.
